# Projects

## 01 · AI Knowledge Assistant with Human-in-the-Loop

### Internal Knowledge

**What if your employees could get instant answers — even when the AI doesn't know the answer?**

### Problem

Employees repeatedly ask colleagues or experts the same questions. Valuable knowledge remains distributed across people instead of becoming reusable organizational knowledge.

### Solution

An AI agent first searches the company's knowledge base using RAG and Qdrant.

If a reliable answer is found, the agent responds immediately.

If no reliable answer is available, the question is escalated to an expert. The confirmed answer is then added to the knowledge base, turning unanswered questions into new organizational knowledge.

### Workflow

```text
Employee question
        ↓
   AI Agent
        ↓
RAG / Knowledge Search
        ↓
   Answer found?
      ↙       ↘
    Yes        No
     ↓          ↓
   Answer   Expert Review
                ↓
        Confirmed Answer
                ↓
        Update Knowledge Base

Technologies

n8n · OpenAI · RAG · Qdrant · OpenAI Embeddings · Google Sheets · Telegram

02 · AI Voice Support Agent
Voice Interface

What if your support team could get product information by voice?

Problem

Support employees need fast access to product information and availability.

Manual searching through tables and systems slows down responses.

Solution

A voice-enabled AI agent accepts voice or text requests, understands requests in multiple languages, searches product information and returns the answer as text or voice.

Workflow

Voice / Text Request
        ↓
Input Processing
        ↓
Speech-to-Text
        ↓
Input Normalization
        ↓
    AI Agent
        ↓
 Product Search
        ↓
 Answer Generation
        ↓
Text / Voice Response

Technologies

n8n · Telegram · OpenRouter · ChatGPT-4 · 11Labs · Google Sheets · Qdrant

Key Concepts
Voice-first support
Multilingual AI
Product knowledge search
Automated responses

03 · AI Multi-Agent Support System
E-Commerce Support

What if your online store could handle most support requests automatically?

Not one chatbot — a coordinated AI support system with specialized agents, human escalation and automated quality control.

Problem

An online store receives product, order, return and warranty questions.

Employees manually classify requests, search for information and prepare responses.

Solution

A Router Agent identifies the request type and sends it to a specialized AI agent.

Complex or uncertain cases are escalated to a human operator.

AI-generated responses are then evaluated by a separate Evaluation Agent and logged for quality monitoring.

Workflow

Customer Request
        ↓
   Router Agent
        ↓
 ┌──────┼───────────────┐
 ↓      ↓               ↓
Product & Order    Returns &      Human Support
Agent              Warranty Agent
 └──────┬───────────────┘
        ↓
   AI Response
        ↓
 Evaluation Agent
        ↓
    Quality Log

Technologies

n8n · OpenRouter · ChatGPT-4 · Telegram · Google Sheets · Qdrant / Vector Store

Key Concepts
Multi-agent architecture
Intelligent routing
Human escalation
Automated evaluation
Quality monitoring
04 · Privacy-Safe LLM Workflow
Privacy & Compliance

What if your company could use LLMs without exposing sensitive data?

Problem

AI applications may need to process personally identifiable or sensitive information.

Sending such data directly to an external LLM can create privacy and compliance risks.

Solution

The workflow identifies sensitive information and replaces it with tokens before the data reaches the LLM.

A risk gate determines whether processing can continue.

If the workflow is considered safe, the LLM processes the tokenized data. The original values can then be restored.

Unsafe requests are blocked or sent for human review.

Workflow

Dataset
   ↓
PII Detection / Tokenization
   ↓
 Risk Gate
   ↓
 ┌───────────────┴───────────────┐
 ↓                               ↓
Safe                          Not Safe
 ↓                               ↓
LLM Processing              Block / Human Review
 ↓
Restore Tokens
 ↓
Final Output

Technologies

n8n · PII Tokenization · Risk Gate · LLM · Data Protection

Key Concepts
PII protection
Tokenization
Risk-based processing
Human review
Privacy-aware LLM workflows
05 · AI Legal Navigator
Legal Operations

What if your legal team could automate routine questions and route complex cases to the right person?

Problem

Legal teams receive repetitive questions, but different requests require different actions:

information search
document-related tasks
consultation
specialist involvement
Solution

The AI agent analyzes the request and routes it to the appropriate workflow.

Relevant information can be retrieved from the corporate knowledge base using RAG and Qdrant.

Workflow

User Request
      ↓
AI Legal Navigator
      ↓
Request Classification
      ↓
Appropriate Workflow
      ↓
Knowledge Retrieval / Action
      ↓
Response or Human Escalation

Technologies

n8n · OpenRouter · LLM · RAG · Qdrant · OpenAI Embeddings · Telegram · Gmail · Google Sheets

Key Concept

One entry point → intelligent routing → specialized workflows → relevant answer or human escalation.

06 · AI Feedback Triage
Customer Feedback

What if AI could decide which customer feedback needs human attention?

Problem

Customer feedback must be read, classified and prioritized.

As volume increases, manual review becomes slower and important issues can be missed.

Solution

The AI analyzes incoming feedback, validates the input and assigns a confidence / priority level.

Different confidence levels determine the next action.

Workflow

Customer Feedback
        ↓
Input Validation
        ↓
   AI Analysis
        ↓
Confidence Assessment
        ↓
 ┌────────┼─────────┐
 ↓        ↓         ↓
High    Medium      Low
 ↓        ↓         ↓
Auto    Human      Request
Response Review   More Info
        ↓
   Google Sheets
        ↓
       Log

Technologies

n8n · OpenRouter · AI Agent · Google Sheets

Key Concepts
AI triage
Confidence-based routing
Human-in-the-loop
Automated logging
07 · Lead Generation & AI Qualification
Lead Generation

What if your business could turn AI conversations into qualified leads?

AI conversations become structured, qualified and measurable lead data.

Challenge

Potential customers interact with AI, but valuable lead information can remain inside the conversation.

Solution

An AI Agent answers questions using a RAG knowledge base, identifies potential leads and automatically submits structured lead data to the business.

Workflow

User
 ↓
AI Agent
 ↓
RAG / Qdrant
 ↓
Intent Analysis
 ↓
Lead Qualification
 ↓
Submit Lead
 ↓
┌──────────────┬──────────────┐
↓              ↓              ↓
Google Sheets  Gmail       Telegram

Technologies

n8n · AI Agent · Qdrant · RAG · OpenRouter · Google Sheets · Webhooks · Gmail · Telegram

Supporting Workflows
Lead Delivery

Submitted lead data is delivered through a webhook to multiple business channels at the same time:

Google Sheets
Gmail
Telegram

This separates lead generation from lead delivery and allows the captured data to be routed to the systems used by the business.

Automated AI Quality Control

A scheduled workflow runs test cases against the AI agent.

A Judge Agent with access to the knowledge base evaluates each answer, scores the result, logs the evaluation and alerts when the score drops below the defined threshold.

Scheduled Test Cases
        ↓
     AI Agent
        ↓
   Generated Answer
        ↓
    Judge Agent
        ↓
      Score
        ↓
     Log Result
        ↓
Score below threshold?
      ↙       ↘
    No         Yes
     ↓           ↓
 Continue      Alert

Technologies

n8n · Judge Agent · Qdrant · Embeddings · Google Sheets · Webhooks · Gmail · Telegram

